# Wrapper: minimal upstream surface

Goal: keep SmartTublex maintainable when the upstream SmartTube APK artifact is refreshed via apk2maven.

## Prefer isolation (in order)

1. **SmartTublex-only files/modules** — new classes under `com.smarttublex.*`, `:app`, `PlexServiceCore/`, registries/helpers owned by this repo
2. **Inheritance / overrides** — subclass public upstream types (`MainApplication`, presenters, activities) and override hooks
3. **Avoid** editing decompiled upstream bytecode, re-shipping patched upstream sources, or large copy-paste of upstream classes

## Upstream = APK artifact

- Upstream is the Maven artifact produced by apk2maven (`com.liskovsoft.smarttubetv:smarttube`), not a git merge of yuliskov source
- Do not modify classes inside the installed JAR/APK
- Sync means reload + reinstall the artifact (see [artifact-sync skill](../skills/artifact-sync/SKILL.md) and [ARTIFACT_SYNC.md](../../fork-docs/ARTIFACT_SYNC.md))

## When adding a customization point

- Prefer a SmartTublex class + thin override call site
- Document new wrapper touch points in [fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md](../../fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md) § Wrapper Touch Points
- Mark non-obvious overrides with a short comment: `// WRAPPER: <why>`

## Decision check (before coding)

- Can this live in a SmartTublex-only class with a small override? → do that
- Unsure whether to subclass a large upstream type? → propose the smaller-diff option first; wait for confirmation on broader overrides
